{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-c__dev-v006-2A-D/bemf-coast/capture-1",
  "notes": "compensation grades the board's terms for a low-speed current reading and the dynamic two-zero tracker against the stage 1 captures and the stage 2 bemf-coast datasets of mg90-c (capture-1, capture-2, low-1, low-meter-3) and mg90-b (capture-1). awake_step_*: the open bridge 1-20 ms after each coast cut over the cycle's torque-off baseline mean, per rail, mg90-c, the bounds one standard error over the coasts; awake_step_mg90b_counts the same on mg90-b. asleep_zero_counts: the baseline mean per rail. step_shape: the fits of the step against the coast's rail per spin. switching_share: the dropout rows and the dummy's slow-decay trough over the open bridge. tracker_replay: the tick-exact port through each dataset's timeline, the error of the awake zero against the dataset's own per-rail open bridge; warm = the dataset's first chain left out; the primary replay feeds the dummy's trough level with a 20 ms brake, the variants the dropout level (e), the open bridge (b) and a 1 s brake. convergence: the exact port under continuous dithered feed. methods_pooled: A the tracker, B0 the tracker + slope x (rail - rail at the last feed), B with a rail EWMA, C the asleep zero + mg90-c capture-1's three-rail table by the live rail, Cline the same with the line; warm, the last 200 ms. recommended_form: C as the seed on a rail change, the tracker trimming. board_terms: each term in rev/s at low speed through mg90-c's own R and Ke. motor_constants: mg90-c's from its own stall pass and coasts, mg90-b's from its stage 2 results.",
